%S A400922 1,1,2,6,20,69,257,988,3900,15738,64581,268672,1130693,4804808,
%T A400922 20587994,88854104,385898644,1685306216,7396489878,32605260910,
%U A400922 144302156477,640938804587,2856122812943,12765278562164,57209589064643,257038080134767,1157529846253063
%N A400922 Number of monosubstituted acyclic hydrocarbons (alkanes and olefins), taking stereoisomers into account.
%C A400922 Equivalent to the number of rooted multigraph trees, in which each node has out-degree <= 4, each edge has multiplicity <= 2, and no node is adjacent to two edges both with multiplicity 2. In the chemical interpretation, the final restriction excludes allenes and cumulenes, which have low stability compared to the classes considered here.
%C A400922 Ignoring stereoisomers means that the children of a node are unordered. They can be permuted in any way and it is still the same tree. See A400921 for the analogous sequence with stereoisomers counted.
%C A400922 A000625 is the analogous sequence considering only alkanes.
%H A400922 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A400922/b400922.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400922 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen and Daniel Merkle, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02932">Enumerating Chemical Structures, Stereoisomers, and Stereogenic Units with Analytic Combinatorics</a>, arXiv:2609.02932 [physics.chem-ph], 2026.
%H A400922 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen, <a href="https://gitlab.com/casbjorn/molenum">Python Notebook</a> (0.2.0).
%F A400922 G.f.: A(x) satisfies A(x) = 1 + x*((1 + 3*x)*A(x)^3 + 2*A(x^3))/3. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 22 2026
%o A400922 (PARI) seq(n) = {my(g=O(1)); for(n=0, n, g = 1 + x*((1+3*x)*g^3 + 2*subst(g,x,x^3))/3 ); Vec(g)} \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 22 2026
%Y A400922 Cf. A000625, A400921, A400923.
%K A400922 nonn,new
